From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chris <08a487@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:22:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/21] power: supply: qcom_fg: Don't log a deferred battery
 registration as an error

power_supply_register() can defer while the battery's supplier is not
ready yet; dev_err_probe() keeps that quiet and records the reason.
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
index db45f7417..267e27e2a 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
@@ -1142,10 +1142,9 @@ static int qcom_fg_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	chip->batt_psy = devm_power_supply_register(chip->dev,
 			&batt_psy_desc, &supply_config);
-	if (IS_ERR(chip->batt_psy)) {
-		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Failed to register battery\n");
-		return PTR_ERR(chip->batt_psy);
-	}
+	if (IS_ERR(chip->batt_psy))
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, PTR_ERR(chip->batt_psy),
+				     "Failed to register battery\n");
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, chip);
 
